WEBVTT

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:10.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the thirteenth. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.379
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, you're there. Anyone see the football last night? Honestly, that second half.</v>

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.949
<v Jamie Brennan>Unfortunately. I'd just about stopped being annoyed, so cheers for that.</v>

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:28.859
<v Grace Liu>I've had traffic on the ring road to be annoyed about instead. Absolutely solid this morning.</v>

00:00:30.969 --> 00:00:33.070
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely start to a Monday, then.</v>

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:40.890
<v Fiona Doyle>And the heating in the portakabin's doing its tropical setting again. I'm sat here with the door open.</v>

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:45.969
<v Priya Raman>You're a bit muffled. Is your headset under your coat?</v>

00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:52.969
<v Fiona Doyle>No, scarf. There. Purely a moan about the heating, by the way, not a maintenance request.</v>

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.640
<v Aisha Begum>That's clearer. Can almost hear the heat escaping.</v>

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get onto what's needed, anything already closed out?</v>

00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:07.450
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I signed off the inspection on the GT2 on Tuesday. Last Tuesday, obviously.</v>

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.890
<v Sarah Okafor>That's fully closed, then? Not another inspection outstanding?</v>

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.290
<v Grace Liu>Fully closed. Just keeping it out of today's list.</v>

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:23.060
<v Jamie Brennan>And I finished the repair on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot last night. That's done.</v>

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.150
<v Tomasz Nowak>Look at you, escaping Stores and everything.</v>

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:32.989
<v Jamie Brennan>Don't get used to it. But yes, finished, no carry-over on that repair.</v>

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:39.349
<v Grace Liu>While I'm on, I heard a slight rattle from the Stretch Wrapper, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:42.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observation only. Not putting a job against that.</v>

00:01:44.319 --> 00:01:51.670
<v Aisha Begum>Same sort of thing here: heard a slight rattle from the line 1, nothing to action yet. Just something I noticed.</v>

00:01:52.379 --> 00:01:56.230
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, a noise mentioned on a call isn't automatically a strip-down.</v>

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:03.810
<v Priya Raman>On the blocked stuff, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve.</v>

00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:10.500
<v Fiona Doyle>So that remains blocked, rather than becoming work we can actually put through today.</v>

00:02:12.229 --> 00:02:17.129
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Status hasn't changed. I'm not adding a separate chase to this morning's actions.</v>

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:24.189
<v Aisha Begum>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line 3 chiller. Same position there.</v>

00:02:25.689 --> 00:02:29.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Both still blocked, no new action coming out of those updates.</v>

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:38.479
<v Jamie Brennan>Also, we were going to replace the belt on the CV01 but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:46.069
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, that's off today's work. Not sitting there as something someone needs to pick up.</v>

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:55.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Fiona, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the site water for tomorrow morning? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:02:57.639 --> 00:03:04.990
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, no, I can't take that. I'm already at capacity, and I can't give the isolation side the attention it needs.</v>

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:14.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, not with Fiona, then. Grace, can you take over sorting the permit to work and isolation for the site water?</v>

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:21.280
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the site water for tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.930
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, just checking—you're taking both bits, not only the permit paperwork?</v>

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.949
<v Grace Liu>Both, yeah. The permit to work and the isolation. That's with me.</v>

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:37.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace. That one's safety critical, straight away, with it sorted for tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:37.669 --> 00:03:39.770
<v Grace Liu>Understood. Straight away on that one.</v>

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:47.330
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:52.490
<v Aisha Begum>Sarah, that's you taking the recalibration itself, yeah?</v>

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:57.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll do the recalibration. I'm not handing that one round.</v>

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:04.550
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right. Sensors, rather than a mechanical overhaul of the valve. Easy for those to get muddled in the notes.</v>

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:11.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Recalibrate the sensors on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve, that's the scope.</v>

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:21.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya Raman, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the relief valve at half two? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:04:23.209 --> 00:04:28.110
<v Priya Raman>Yes, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the relief valve at half two.</v>

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.439
<v Fiona Doyle>Half two for the sign-off itself, rather than just starting to look at it?</v>

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.060
<v Priya Raman>For the sign-off, yes. At half two. I've got that.</v>

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:46.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. It's production-holding work, so it stays a first-priority job, not something tucked behind the routine stuff.</v>

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:53.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you schedule downtime for the line 1 TCU with production on Friday? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:55.470 --> 00:05:00.019
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll schedule downtime for the line 1 TCU with production on Friday.</v>

00:05:01.759 --> 00:05:05.959
<v Aisha Begum>That's arranging the downtime, not taking on the actual maintenance as well?</v>

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:11.009
<v Sarah Okafor>Just scheduling the downtime with production. Nothing else being added to it.</v>

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:17.079
<v Jamie Brennan>Fine, that's with me. On Friday, and not an urgent one.</v>

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.089
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, that makes sense. Not treating that as an urgent outage.</v>

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:32.100
<v Grace Liu>There's still the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet. Those need doing Monday, so today. We haven't got anyone against that.</v>

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet for Monday?</v>

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.589
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't commit to those, sorry.</v>

00:05:42.439 --> 00:05:48.389
<v Jamie Brennan>No, I can't take them either. Don't put my name down just because I mentioned the robot.</v>

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:55.250
<v Sarah Okafor>No, understood. Nobody's taken the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet. Still needed Monday, still unassigned.</v>

00:05:56.069 --> 00:06:02.019
<v Grace Liu>One other thing I can take: I'll inspect the turbine two water valve for leaks by Thursday.</v>

00:06:03.889 --> 00:06:07.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace. That one's whenever you get a chance, by Thursday.</v>

00:06:09.759 --> 00:06:15.709
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll fit that inspection in whenever I get a chance, and have it done by Thursday.</v>

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:22.420
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, I spoke over you there. That's the less urgent one, separate from the site water isolation?</v>

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:32.240
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. The site water permit and isolation is the safety-critical one, straight away. The turbine two water valve inspection is whenever I get a chance, by Thursday.</v>

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:43.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. We've agreed those owners; the Forklift Fleet checks are the exception, still nobody on them. Supplier items remain blocked, and the belt replacement isn't today's work.</v>

00:06:44.519 --> 00:06:48.720
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, that's how I've understood it. Nothing extra from the rattles either.</v>

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:52.189
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. And apparently no sympathy for the football.</v>

00:06:53.149 --> 00:06:55.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely none. Cheers, everyone, we'll leave it there.</v>
